# Space-Track redistribution policy (task G-05, D-01).
#
# USSPACECOM grants blanket approval to redistribute "basic SSA data" (TLE, OMM, SATCAT,
# decay data) *with citation*, so our derived products are publishable. The User Agreement
# (10 USC 2274(c)(2)) still says not to transfer received data or its analysis to third
# parties without approval, and the practical rule we follow is: cite Space-Track, publish
# derived products, do not mirror bulk raw catalogue pulls in a repository.
data/raw/spacetrack/

# Credentials. Also covered by the repo-root .gitignore, repeated here so this directory
# is safe on its own if it is ever moved or vendored.
.env
*.credentials
secrets.*

# Generated
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
*.pyc

# JPL ephemeris kernels (large binaries, re-downloadable from NAIF)
data/raw/ephemeris/*.bsp

# Large third-party datasets (re-downloadable; also keeps them out of git)
data/raw/adsb/
data/raw/ais/
data/raw/goes/
data/raw/literature/
